  "ladder_summary": "Ablation ladder (nasdaq10, quarterly, dividends reinvested), window 2006-01-03 -> 2026-06-12 (~20.4y), all measured vs QQQ. Top-1 single biggest name is the trivial start; each concentration step (top-1 -> top-3 -> top-5 -> top-10) is the big mover. Equal-weight vs cap-weight (WEIGHTING) and full vs drift_band vs no_sell (the REBALANCING RULE) move the needle far less; cost (5bps) and tax (20/37) only subtract. Clean top-10 cap-weight = 1.36x QQQ before frictions.",
  "carrier_hypothesis": "CONCENTRATION is the carrier layer: simply stepping off QQQ into a cap-weighted NASDAQ mega-cap basket is the whole edge -- the trivial top-1 name already jumps to 1.42x QQQ (+2.0 CAGR pts) and the clean top-10 holds 1.36x; everything above (weighting, friction) is second-order. The rebalancing RULE -- the thing in the title -- is among the SMALLEST levers: full/drift/no_sell span only 1.69 CAGR pts and every alternative to 'full' is dominated. The edge over QQQ is OWNING the concentrated basket, not how you rebalance it."
